{
  "title": "Walter Gropius",
  "body": "Walter Adolph Georg Gropius (18 May 1883 – 5 July 1969) was a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Germans\">German</a><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Architect\">architect</a> and founder of the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bauhaus\">Bauhaus</a> School, who, along with <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ludwig_Mies_van_der_Rohe\">Ludwig Mies van der Rohe</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Le_Corbusier\">Le Corbusier</a> and <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Lloyd_Wright\">Frank Lloyd Wright</a>, is widely regarded as one of the pioneering masters of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modern_architecture\">modern architecture</a>.",
